 # Auth: Delegation Tokens, Space Credentials, and App Gating
+
+## Request proofs: proposed foundation (2026-10-15)
+
+No production route enables this extension. This status supersedes the older
+implementation claims below; their historical spec pin is not deployment evidence.
+Stratos currently supports delegation ingestion, credential issuance, optional app
+gating, and local `cnf.jkt`/DPoP reads. Standard transport migration is separate.
+
+### Proposed request binding
+
+`Stratos-Request-Proof` uses an ephemeral P-256 key bound by validated `cnf.kid`,
+without a registered client DID. Where required, `Stratos-Service-Assertion` uses
+an issuer-controlled published DID method to bind the exact proof digest. No new
+key purpose is required. Standard Spaces HTTP Message Signatures stay unchanged.
+The candidate contains helpers and injected admission composition, not route enforcement.
+
+Credential, client, service, and authorization checks precede one replay-consumed
+proof identity. The assertion has no second `jti`. Shared state must be atomic and
+retained through expiry plus skew. State loss removes replay protection for
+consumed identities. An unused stolen delegation can still win issuance.
+Possession is not permission or human consent. The PDS remains trusted.
+
+### Audience and integration checklist
+
+- Delegation targets `authorityDid#atproto_space_host`.
+- Standard credential presentation targets the repository owner or authority,
+  as required by the operation.
+- The extension targets the receiving Stratos authority DID. Do not require it
+  on foreign PDS hosts.
+
+Foundation validation covers shared Redis replay tests, scoped mutation testing,
+Terra Standards and Spec reviews, AtmosphereInABox baseline and alignment scenarios,
+and docs CI. This is not production enforcement evidence or an exact-SHA
+AtmosphereInABox run of the later prose overlay. Production ingress, `cnf.kid`
+migration, route enforcement, and operational replay retention still need evidence.
+Rust vector consumption belongs to Plan 015.
+
 
